    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.63,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.6 from 7 h onward, which could have been detector saturation hiding continued growth. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test this. The ×10 dilution read 0.168, which scales to 1.68. The ×5 dilution read 0.322, which scales to 1.61. The undiluted reading was 1.553. The three estimates agree within about 8%, and the ×5 and ×10 reads differ from each other by about 4%. If the reader were saturating, the diluted samples would scale to well above the undiluted reading, for example 3 or more. They do not. Any shortfall in the undiluted reading is small, about 4–8%, and is comparable to the noise in the plateau readings. The plateau is therefore real stationary phase at an OD of about 1.6, and the biomass is as the readings indicate. This rests on one replicate per dilution because of the budget."
  },
